The Marksman is the neutral elite of the Hunter (ranger route; no alignment
asked). It is the critical-hit archer: its shots land harder, its Aimed Shot
comes back sooner, and a good shot hobbles its target.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Called Shot       its shots have +15% critical chance, and its
                       critical hits deal 50% more damage
  35 Quicker aim       Aimed Shot is ready another round sooner
  40 Pinning Crit      an Aimed Shot that lands hobbles the target for
                       2 rounds
  45 Back-line eye     +10 Attack against foes in the back row
  50 Unblockable       its critical hits can not be blocked
  55 Second Nock       an Aimed Shot that fells its target shoots again
                       at a new target, once a round
  60 Perfect Shot      its first Aimed Shot each battle can not miss or
                       be avoided

Called Shot's extra critical chance needs a shooting weapon in hand; the
other ranks work with any weapon. Aimed Shot is already a sure critical hit
when it lands, so Called Shot works through the Marksman's other shots and the
extra critical damage. The Second Nock's arrow is an ordinary shot.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Ranger elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Long Draw (+10% damage with a
shooting weapon), Eagle Eye (+5 Attack with a shooting weapon), Quick Nock
(+15 opening action meter). Every elite ranger may take them. See <ansi
fg="command">help talents</ansi>.


